==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|non|svara||to answer}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*swarōną}}, cognate to {{cog|en|answer|an'''swer'''}}. Compare {{m|sv|svar||a response}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/ˈsvɑːˌra/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-svara.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-reg}}

# to [[answer]], to [[reply]], to [[respond]]

====Usage notes====
* The [[past participle]] form is very rare.
* The difference to the word {{m|sv|besvara}} lies in that {{m|sv|svara}} concerns answers or responses to people, while {{m|sv|besvara}} (or in some cases {{m|sv|svara}} + certain particles) concerns answers or responses to questions, telephone calls and so on:
*: ''Att '''besvara''' en fråga.'' (= ''Att '''svara på''' en fråga.'')
*:: ''To '''answer''' a question.''
*: '''''Svara''' inte '''i''' telefonen när det åskar!''
*:: ''Don't '''answer''' the phone during a thunderstorm!''
*: '''''Svara''' honom inte!''
*:: ''Don't '''answer''' him!''

